proc: set up the Go image when attaching to a non-Go process

Delve stops the target when shared libraries are loaded until it sees a Go image
being loaded. When attaching, the Go image is already loaded, so the first library
loaded afterwards (e.g. an NSS module during a DNS or user lookup) stops the
process inside the dynamic linker, which IDEs report as a breakpoint hit in an
unknown location. Set up the Go image when attaching.

